+# Packing outside macOS (Linux)
+
+`scripts/build_ipa_from_nsp.py` also runs on Linux. Everything up to the shader split is the same code as on the Mac; these stand in for Xcode:
+
+| Mac | Linux |
+| --- | --- |
+| `xcrun -sdk iphoneos metal` / `metallib` (the shader chain) | `dm/linux/bin/xcrun`: Apple's **Metal Developer Tools for Windows** under wine, with `-target air64-apple-ios<min>` for the SDK |
+| `build_ipa.sh` (bash) and `gen_build.py` (`make -n`) | `dm/ios/tools/build_ipa_portable.py` and `gen_build_portable.py`: the same steps in Python, the compile list evaluated from `dm/host/Makefile` itself (no bash, no make); Windows too |
+| `xcodegen` + `xcodebuild` | `dm/ios/tools/build_app_linux.py`: clang + `ld64.lld` against an iPhoneOS SDK taken from `Xcode.xip`; the icon as PNG files named in Info.plist (no `actool`) |
+| Xcode's Swift compiler (the app's `Launcher.swift`) | the Linux Swift toolchain's `swiftc` with Xcode's Swift resource folder (`DM_SWIFT_RESOURCES`: the toolchain's `usr/lib/swift`, its `iphoneos` part, `apinotes` and clang headers suffice) |
+| `dm/gfx/tools/dmsh_xlate_bin/dmsh_xlate` (a macOS launcher) | the same `dmsh_xlate.dll` run with `dotnet` (the NSP script writes a launcher in `<id>_build/tools/dmsh_xlate`) |
+| Arial Unicode / Arial Rounded Bold (shared-font stand-ins) | Noto Sans / Noto Sans Bold, else DejaVu Sans (`STD_FONT`, `LETTER_FONT` override them) |
+
+The shaders build through `dm/gfx/tools/own_compilers.py` as on the Mac: the distribution's spirv-cross and the Windows metal differ from
+`dmsh_chain.lock` and are named in one note line; the translator must still be the locked build, and the chain version stays the repository's.
+Steps that boot the game in the Mac host (a run-time shader capture, a decode with the game's own Oodle or LZ5, a provisional profile's heap
+check) need a Mac with Apple silicon and are not available here. `--prepare-xcode` needs Xcode and stops.
+
+## Setup
+
+1. Python with `lz4 capstone fonttools pillow` (`backports.zstd` before 3.14; Pillow writes the app icon).
+2. Packages: `dotnet` (SDK 10), `spirv-cross`, `zstd`, `clang` and `lld` (`ld64.lld`), `make`, `wine`, `swift` (the app has Swift sources).
+3. The iOS SDK: `DM_IOS_SDK=<iPhoneOS.sdk folder>` (e.g. extracted from Xcode 26's `.xip` by nxnativev2), or xtool's Darwin SDK (`xtool sdk install <Xcode.xip>`), which is looked up by default.
+4. The Metal compiler: **Metal Developer Tools for Windows** (6.x) installed with wine; `dm/linux/bin/xcrun` looks under
+   `$WINEPREFIX/drive_c/Program Files/Metal Developer Tools`, or `DM_METAL_WIN=<folder>`. Check: `dm/linux/bin/xcrun -sdk iphoneos metal --version`.
+
+Then: `python3 scripts/build_ipa_from_nsp.py <NSP folder> -k <prod.keys>`. The IPA is unsigned.
